# Commands and results

`scripts/coverage-gate.ps1` passed: 55 protobuf types, 131 field fixtures, 55 explicit-zero fixtures, 6 corrupt frames, 19 categories, 11 developer frames, 10 client responses, 26 incoming frames; unit, race and vet all exited 0. `scripts/build-windows.ps1` exited 0 and produced the packaged EXE/DLL. The final 180-second live smoke exited 1 because the target did not establish a 9421 upstream connection after successful listener startup, Frida attach, and CDP connect.

# Skipped checks

Live upstream smoke is the only skipped/pass-blocking environment check for this revision; its failure is recorded as a real result, not a pass.

# Spec consistency

The implementation scope covers the Go runtime, embedded Frida Agent, pinned address configurations, WMPF/CDP protocol implementation, tests, fixtures, Windows build scripts, project documentation, and license notices.

# Known limitations and risks

Windows is the first supported platform. Live smoke verification depends on a running compatible target process and its upstream debug connection.

# Conclusion

The reference behavior matrix is 100% mapped to executable fixtures/tests. Native Windows upstream smoke still requires a target session that opens the WMPF debug socket.
